    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Choice A — Teaching Tips (Polish the Style)\r\n\r\n- **Keep the work incremental.**  \r\n  Encourage students to improve one interactive element at a time (nav links, then buttons, then card links). Preview between changes.\r\n\r\n- **Push for clear, specific requirements before prompting.**  \r\n  If students jump straight into AI, redirect them to quickly define their goal, constraints (brand + readability), and what could go wrong.\r\n\r\n- **Watch for “polish” that hurts usability.**  \r\n  Remind students to check that interactive elements are still easy to identify and read (contrast, clarity, consistency), not just more decorative. Encourage them to briefly resize the preview to confirm the design still works on smaller screens.\r\n\r\n- **Encourage review before saving.**  \r\n  Ask: “What changed, and why does it matter for the user?” Require a short version comment that names the improvement (not just “updated CSS”).",
